# P5-002 pinned artwork assessment and coverage

Owner reports Jagex permission for third-party icon sourcing and bundling in **this private local planner**. This is **Owner-provided permission**, not independently verified. It grants no independently established broader distribution rights. Repository notices and underlying Jagex/Wiki rights remain applicable. Nothing here licenses the whole planner under a new license or authorizes publication/deployment.

## Assessed and adopted sources

| Source | Pinned revision | Assessment/use |
|---|---|---|
| [osrsbox/osrsbox-db](https://github.com/osrsbox/osrsbox-db) | `dae12e3400add0c71465f07a334f9d8f86bebce8` | Revision metadata dates to 2021-09-30; currency is not assumed. Selected item and prayer PNG data was matched by explicit stable IDs/exact names. 29 item icons and 29 prayer icons adopted. Duplicate/LMS/animation/ornament/degraded variants were not selected automatically. Chosen charged/active/undamaged representations are recorded per match. |
| [Dava96/osrs-icons](https://github.com/Dava96/osrs-icons) | `16c5de73d6c57e1b47ef0606cf4b6e4ff39e82c6` | Revision metadata dates to 2026-09-22. Selected PNG exports were decoded as data only; no upstream TypeScript/package code executed or installed. Supplies skills, a missing item (Osmumten's fang), activity logos and generic category markers. Beta/LMS/ornament/version-suffixed alternatives were explicitly excluded where a normal named export was chosen. |

Original notices copied verbatim to `public/notices/artwork/`: both LICENSE and README files. osrsbox's GPL-3.0 source notice has explicit Jagex-art and Wiki-content exceptions; selected game-art bytes are not represented as GPL-owned project code. Dava96 declares CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 and credits Jagex/Wiki contributors. Preserve the attribution, noncommercial/share-alike notice and [license URI](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/3.0/legalcode). Extracted PNG bytes are unchanged; base64/CSS containers were removed, with no resizing/recoloring. No upstream software dependency was adopted.

The source notices do not independently verify the Owner's Jagex permission. The private scope and absence of broader distribution authorization remain explicit. Original fallback symbols and legacy test-asset notices are unchanged.

## Actual coverage

94 unique PNGs, **60,053 bytes**, cover 207 catalog records as follows:

| Category | Records | Identity-specific authentic icon | Generic authentic category marker | Original fallback used by default |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Skills | 24 | 24 | 0 | 0 |
| Items | 30 | 30 | 0 | 0 |
| Prayers | 29 | 29 | 0 | 0 |
| Activities | 20 | 7 | 13 | 0 |
| Quests | 32 | 0 | 32 | 0 |
| Bosses | 24 | 0 | 24 | 0 |
| Diary tiers | 48 | 0 | 48 | 0 |
| **Total** | **207** | **90** | **117** | **0** |

Generic markers are intentionally disclosed: quest-start marker for quests; combat-achievements marker for bosses; achievement-diary cape for diary categories; minigame marker for activities without a selected named logo. They do **not** depict individual quests/boss portraits/diary regions or tiers. These 117 identity-specific-art gaps are not claimed as exact visual matches. Catalog completeness/newest-content and a live audit of all reference links remain separate gaps.

Reviewed mappings live in `artwork-selection.json`; every catalog ID has an explicit source ID/export, match scope and basis. `artwork-manifest.json` records full revisions, source paths/URLs, provenance, permissions, PNG dimensions/SHA-256 and per-category counts. All 94 images decode in the real-browser test and were inspected in a contact sheet. No fuzzy runtime matching occurs. Missing/unknown assets retain the original fallback; existing manual overrides (including original symbols and legacy references) win over new defaults.

## Repeatable preparation/update

No package installation is needed. `scripts/prepare-artwork.mjs` uses Node built-ins, validates pinned input hashes and PNG signatures/dimensions, extracts data without executing upstream code, and writes only selected PNGs, generated lookup/manifest and notices. It never accesses a player's roadmap or browser storage.

```powershell
node scripts/prepare-artwork.mjs --check
# Use --cache <directory> for a different cache. On a fresh machine:
node scripts/prepare-artwork.mjs --cache evidence/my-new-art-cache --fetch
node scripts/prepare-artwork.mjs --cache evidence/my-new-art-cache --check
```

Default cache is the preserved P5-002 assessment directory. `--fetch` only retrieves the eight whitelisted raw files at the pinned revisions; network permission may be required. Actual assessment downloads were performed, and cached generation/check ran successfully. A fresh-cache invocation of the final tool's `--fetch` branch was not separately rerun. Public app runtime is entirely local; no CDN/API requests.

For an update: assess new source notices/revisions, review exact mappings and variants, intentionally update `inputHashes` and pins, prepare in a separate review checkout/output before replacing existing assets. The tool refuses a differing existing PNG instead of silently overwriting it. Verify generated metadata/notices/hashes and run tests. Keep stable catalog IDs. The generated default-art lookup does not rewrite goal titles, IDs, statuses, hidden counters, positions, groups, connections or overrides. Existing asset files remain available for saved explicit overrides; do not remove them without a separate compatibility decision. Distribution beyond the private planner needs a separate rights decision.
